assistant: Subject: parse epoch-millisecond created_at in get_order

Nothing in shop-mcp caused the alert's 404, and nothing in it can fix that 404. `create_order` returned `{"order_id":"o-5002","status":"confirmed","total":1499}`, which matches the vendor's 200 response exactly. The vendor's own `GET /orders/o-5002` then returned 404 for an order it had just confirmed. shop-mcp only passed that 404 on, so it is a vendor-side issue, and the order should stay "unconfirmed" until the vendor explains it. The one real problem I found in the trace is a different one, and it's the only thing I changed. Vendor version 2026-10-01 sends `created_at` as epoch milliseconds (`1792315539045`) instead of the ISO string in the spec. `get_order` turned that into text and parsed it as a date, which fails and falls back to 0. So once the read-back succeeds, it would report the order as placed in 1970. The fix, in `src/tools/get_order.ts`, uses a numeric `created_at` directly as milliseconds and still parses strings for v1, so the v1 output is unchanged. Typecheck, lint and all 13 tests pass. There are no v2 recordings in the repo, so no test covers the new path. I didn't add an `Idempotency-Key` header or change any upstream request, because nothing shows that would fix the 404 and it would break the strict v1 replays.

